 "t1_us1_shift": "T1|us1 pass lines 27 / 53 -> 36 / 71 microstrain are real: the BL-053 lines were run on the BL-054 print; BL-055 grew the hip boss to D50 x 16 mm (8 inserts), which lies inside the US1 submodel box (+8514 voxels at x -6..25, y -49..-33, z 96..145, 93 mm from the gauge). The stiffer lumbar hub moves the bag-on (drape, -y) load's near-null point at the US1 gauge: the point value goes -0.00019 -> -0.00038 MPa/N (-7 -> -15 microstrain at 150 lb) and the band minimum over the +/-1.5 mm placement tolerance -0.00060 -> -0.00081 MPa/N, which sets the pass line (x 1.15). The same hub costs the MT-1cr|us1 line 4 % (cradle leg: -0.00383 -> -0.00366 MPa/N): at a near-null point the same shift is a large fraction. Re-running the current code on the BL-054 STL gives the old 27 / 53 back; BL-056 and BL-058 (US2 blocks, counterbore) leave US1 unchanged; voxel h 1.0 and GAUGE_TOL 1.5 are unchanged (no raster change). See docs/backlog/BL-060-gauge-republish.md."
